   "title": "Vehicle ahead: distance, closing speed and time to collision vs the car's radar",
   "text": "Pre-registered (evaluation/real/PREREGISTRATION_LEAD.md) on the same comma2k19 segment, a different task: YOLOX-S on OpenCV 5's DNN module finds the vehicle in the ego lane; distance from the ground plane (camera height from the lane-width prior) fused with a vehicle-width ruler; closing speed from the rate at which the vehicle grows in the image. Ground truth is the car's forward radar. The method changed during development; the deviations are listed in the pre-registration. Range is compared after a constant 1.29 m camera-to-radar offset fitted on development. Each ruler alone on the test windows (post hoc, same windows): ground plane only 9.6 %, vehicle width only 2.3 %. The lead car's width is close to the 1.8 m prior, which favours the width ruler.",
